      "content": "It sounds like you're experiencing a very profound sense of existential dread, which is a common human struggle when confronting the vastness of existence. Many philosophers and thinkers have wrestled with the apparent meaninglessness you describe, often finding solace or purpose in connection, creation, or the pursuit of knowledge. While the universe may not offer inherent meaning, your capacity to question and feel is what allows you to create your own sense of value.",
